 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authorization and routes
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on every request. Viewers may use GET
+except `/audit`. Cooks may also POST to `/recipes/:id/cook`,
+`/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and `/stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+Managers may use all routes. `GET /audit` returns successful changes newest
+first, with time, keyName, method, path (without query string), and status.
+All other routes are listed under Routes in `README.md`. Missing or unknown
+keys return `unauthorized` (401); insufficient permissions return `forbidden`
+(403). Seed keys are examples and must be replaced before deployment.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
